commit 59418332e2bfad9a033565c0cf85fb9c450dd654
Author: AI Teammate <agent.ai.native@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 28 19:41:13 2026 +0000

    fix(1947): schedule_message self-reminders no longer misroute into a finished subagent's mailbox

    - ShellJobRegistry binds its settle continuation to the construction-time
      boot zone: a background job started by a child used to fire its
      onSettled (and the CLI idle settle-wake that starts a fresh MAIN run)
      inside the finished child's subagent zone, so activeSubagentId() named
      the child for the whole wake run and every schedule_message in it was
      self-addressed to the child (the gh-1947 report: a timer that
      auto-resumed a completed subagent with duplicate-side-effect risk).
    - Both hosts' scheduleSenderMailbox wiring now trusts the zone scope only
      while that child is genuinely in flight on the session executor
      (TaskExecutor.isInFlight) — any future stale-zone capture degrades to
      the caller's own (main) mailbox instead of a dead child's.
    - The tool response names the recipient the record actually carries: an
      explicit to: used to be shadowed by the sender's mailbox in the reply,
      which read as 'override ignored' even when it was honored.
    - E2E repro through the real AgentCli (child bash background job outlives
      the child, then settles into a MAIN wake run) + registry-level zone pin;
      gh-970 child self-scheduling keeps its in-flight identity.

diff --git a/lib/src/tools/shell_jobs.dart b/lib/src/tools/shell_jobs.dart
index 01241b9..26c5f50 100644
--- a/lib/src/tools/shell_jobs.dart
+++ b/lib/src/tools/shell_jobs.dart
@@ -290,6 +290,16 @@ final class ShellJobRegistry {
   /// options — the size ceiling and the low-disk warning channel; null
   /// bytes means the shells' built-in default. A caller's own options
   /// values take precedence over these session defaults.
+  ///
+  /// The settle continuation is bound to the zone this registry was
+  /// CONSTRUCTED in (host boot), never to the zone of the `bash` call that
+  /// happened to start the job (gh-1947): a job started by a subagent used
+  /// to carry its `onSettled` into the child's subagent zone, so a job
+  /// settling after the child's run ended fired the host's settle path —
+  /// including the idle settle-wake that starts a fresh MAIN run — with
+  /// `activeSubagentId()` still naming the long-finished child. Every
+  /// identity consumer of that run (schedule_message's self-mailbox
+  /// resolution among them) then attributed MAIN's work to the child.
   ShellJobRegistry({
     required this.env,
     this.onStart,
@@ -301,7 +311,8 @@ final class ShellJobRegistry {
     this.jobLogRedactor,
     this.maxRetainedExitedJobs = defaultMaxRetainedExitedJobs,
     DateTime? bootTime,
-  }) : _bootTime = bootTime ?? DateTime.now();
+  }) : _bootTime = bootTime ?? DateTime.now(),
+       _bootZone = Zone.current;

   /// How many exited jobs the registry retains (gh-1438 second tier).
   /// Production monitor sessions ran thousands of short-lived jobs and the
@@ -357,6 +368,10 @@ final class ShellJobRegistry {
   /// Registry creation time; old-format logs modified before it are
   /// historical debris, not a live stale instance.
   final DateTime _bootTime;
+
+  /// The zone the host constructed this registry in (host boot). Settle
+  /// continuations run there — see the constructor doc (gh-1947).
+  final Zone _bootZone;
   var _staleJobLogWarned = false;
   final _jobs = <ShellJobEntry>[];
   var _nextId = 1;
@@ -458,19 +473,27 @@ final class ShellJobRegistry {
       timeout: options?.timeout,
     );
     _jobs.add(entry);
+    // Registered inside [_bootZone], so the settle callback — and the
